[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Red for Danger]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.54]How was the drunk removed from the ring? | 醉汉是怎样被弄出斗牛场的？
[00:15.52]During a bullfight, a drunk suddenly wandered into the middle of the ring. | 在一场斗牛比赛中，一个醉汉突然踉踉跄跄地闯入场中央。
[00:22.10]The crowd began to shout, but the drunk was unaware of the danger. | 人群开始叫喊，但醉汉却没有意识到危险。
[00:28.65]The bull was busy with the matador at the time, | 当时公牛正忙着对付斗牛士，
[00:33.03]but it suddenly caught sight of the drunk who was shouting rude remarks and waving a red cap. | 但它突然瞥见了那个正说着粗话、挥舞着红帽子的醉汉。
[00:41.14]Apparently sensitive to criticism, | 公牛显然对批评很敏感，
[00:44.66]the bull forgot all about the matador and charged at the drunk. | 它把斗牛士全然抛在脑后，直奔醉汉而来。
[00:50.69]The crowd suddenly grew quiet. | 人群突然安静下来。
[00:54.48]The drunk, however, seemed quite sure of himself. | 然而醉汉却似乎胸有成竹。
[00:59.38]When the bull got close to him, he clumsily stepped aside to let it pass. | 当公牛逼近时，他笨拙地闪身让它扑了个空。
[01:06.51]The crowd broke into cheers and the drunk bowed. | 人群爆发出欢呼声，醉汉鞠了一躬。
[01:11.33]By this time, however three men had come into the ring and they quickly dragged the drunk to safety. | 然而这时3个人已进入斗牛场，迅速把醉汉拖到了安全地方。
[01:20.11]Even the bull seemed to feel sorry for him, | 就连公牛似乎也对他感到同情，
[01:23.79]for it looked on sympathetically until the drunk was out of the way before once more turning its attention to the matador. | 它同情地望着醉汉走开，直到他离开了视线，才把注意力重新转向斗牛士。
